      "text": "To find the largest 4-digit integer that is congruent to \\(15 \\pmod{22}\\), we first need to determine the largest 4-digit number and then adjust it to find the corresponding number that satisfies the given congruence condition.\n\nThe largest 4-digit number is 9999. We need to find such a number, say \\(9999 - x\\), where \\(x\\) is the value of the congruence problem. That is, we want \\(9999 - x \\equiv 15 \\pmod{22}\\).\n\nThis simplifies to:\n\\begin{align*}\n9999 - x &\\equiv 15 \\pmod{22} \\\\\n9999 - 15 &\\equiv x \\pmod{22} \\\\\n9984 &\\equiv x \\pmod{22} \\\\\n\\end{align*}\n\nNow we need to find the largest \\(x\\) which is congruent to 9984 modulo 22. We first find the remainder when 9984 is divided by 22. This can be done using the modulus operation.\n\nTo find \\(9984 \\mod 22\\):\n\n\\[\n9984 \\div 22 = 453 \\text{ remainder } 12\n\\]\nSo,\n\\[\n9984 \\equiv 12 \\pmod{22}\n\\]\n\nThis means the largest 4-digit integer \\(x\\) that satisfies the congruence condition is 9984 - 453 times 22 plus 12. Thus, the largest four-digit integer congruent to 15 modulo 22 is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{9584}\n\\]",
